Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Getting started", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c4526081-7c99-4089-8645-a7c00670cc48"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every figure and animation below is already rendered, so you can read the \
notebook end-to-end in the browser without evaluating anything \[LongDash] \
the animated GIFs embedded in each Output cell play directly in the Community \
viewer. If you do want to rerun or tweak the simulations locally, the Input \
cell above each figure contains the exact call. All the packages the code \
needs ship with this post as ",
 StyleBox["trafficjams-packages.zip", "Input"],
 " \[LongDash] download it from ",
 ButtonBox["here",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/k5kgvqqxbo0zcfolp92ny/trafficjams-\
packages.zip?rlkey=w56xsebnw0f8hj57ck186ayhj&st=8pjc9w6p&dl=0"], None},
  ButtonNote->
   "https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/k5kgvqqxbo0zcfolp92ny/trafficjams-packages.\
zip?rlkey=w56xsebnw0f8hj57ck186ayhj&st=8pjc9w6p&dl=0"],
 " or the repo, unzip it into the ",
 StyleBox["same directory as this notebook",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", and then evaluate the next cell once:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.985889998489399*^9, 3.9858900053603888`*^9}, {
  3.985890044894806*^9, 
  3.9858900448950043`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"48252bd9-d8a4-430e-8b8e-\
314568fd92e8"],

Cell["\<\
SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]];
Get[\"IDM.wl\"];
Get[\"Bando.wl\"];
Get[\"LWR.wl\"];
Get[\"PayneWhitham.wl\"];
Get[\"NagelSchreckenberg.wl\"];
Get[\"NagelSchreckenberg2Lane.wl\"];
Get[\"Queueing.wl\"];
Get[\"SignalOptimisation.wl\"];
Get[\"IntersectionControl.wl\"];
Get[\"NetworkAssignment.wl\"];
Get[\"DynamicAssignment.wl\"];
Get[\"AberdeenNetwork.wl\"];
Get[\"CoreAnimations.wl\"];\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"b26ddf76-8267-4fd4-a702-93e1ea68da3a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The full source (including two extra OSM-based Aberdeen simulations that \
aren't bundled here) is on GitHub: ",
 ButtonBox["github.com/mthiel74/TrafficJAms",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/mthiel74/TrafficJAms"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9dc33a20-cceb-4237-8fca-037007c24c17"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Abstract", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"03134b05-9844-4994-8008-b143181c1460"],

Cell["\<\
Traffic jams are the canonical everyday example of an emergent phenomenon: \
each driver follows simple local rules, and the system as a whole \
spontaneously produces stop-and-go waves, phantom jams, shockwaves, and \
city-scale gridlock. Since the 1950s these have been modelled at wildly \
different scales \[LongDash] as a hyperbolic PDE (Lighthill\[Dash]Whitham\
\[Dash]Richards), as individual vehicles following an ODE (Intelligent Driver \
Model, Bando OVM), as a stochastic cellular automaton \
(Nagel\[Dash]Schreckenberg), as a queueing network at intersections, or as a \
convex optimisation problem on a directed graph (Wardrop equilibrium). This \
notebook walks through all of those in turn, each with a short derivation, \
runnable Wolfram-Language code, and a pre-rendered result. The running case \
study is Aberdeen in north-east Scotland \[LongDash] a city whose peculiar \
geography makes it an unusually nice traffic-engineering laboratory.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2745e847-60ae-4942-8ecc-289d7ed57775"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Why model traffic?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1625fabf-df75-4250-87a1-3c6cc2f67a25"],

Cell["\<\
Traffic engineers need quantitative tools to answer questions like: What \
happens to queue lengths on Union Street if we add a bus gate? If the Bridge \
of Don closes for maintenance, does Anderson Drive absorb the flow, or does \
half the city seize up? What is the shortest green phase at Mounthooly that \
still keeps average delay below 30 s? None of these has a closed-form answer, \
but all of them are tractable in simulation once the correct mathematical \
model has been picked for the right spatial scale.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4dbea6cb-dbec-41b9-ae74-d22a06e5cbe2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Traffic is a textbook example of ",
 StyleBox["emergence",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": individual drivers obey simple local rules (don't hit the car in front, \
change lane if you have to brake), yet the population collectively produces \
structures \[LongDash] phantom jams, shockwaves, stop-and-go oscillations, \
city-scale gridlock \[LongDash] that no single driver is aware of creating. \
This makes traffic a natural fit for the hierarchy of models below: a \
continuum PDE captures the coarse behaviour, an ODE per vehicle reveals the \
microscopic instability, and a directed graph plus a convex program describes \
the network-scale equilibrium. Each scale gets something right the others \
can't, and a real-world deployment often stitches several together."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f7c3c869-b697-49a2-a06d-27a7c7bb79f7"],

Cell["\<\
Aberdeen in north-east Scotland is a good running example. It's small enough \
to be tractable (population ~200\[ThinSpace]000, compact historic centre), \
large enough to be interesting (international airport, oil-industry commuter \
flows, a peripheral ring road opened in 2018), and its geography creates \
natural bottlenecks \[LongDash] the Bridge of Don and Bridge of Dee, the \
Haudagain roundabout, the Anderson Drive corridor \[LongDash] that any model \
will want to reproduce.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"87a3615c-7b3e-4a72-b706-e1118c38b624"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. The macroscopic view: the LWR model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0cdfa96b-1fbb-4019-a7d6-d5ec3155e5e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Lighthill and Whitham (1955), followed independently by Richards (1956), \
proposed that traffic on a long road obeys the same conservation law as any \
other compressible one-dimensional fluid: vehicles cannot be created or \
destroyed, so the density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "(", "x", ",", " ", "t", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "82e4521c-17dc-45cc-a7ae-59b4a4a0ba58"],
 " and flow ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Q", "(", "\[Rho]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "37933876-8a7f-4b92-b201-7dde5a7ad98e"],
 " satisfy"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12f4c662-e5fc-4268-b26f-cf58153000ab"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "\[Rho]"}], 
    RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "t"}]], "+", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
     RowBox[{"Q", "(", "\[Rho]", ")"}]}], 
    RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]], "=", "0"}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"b04083fe-ef74-4f2c-8013-d0357e51e6c8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The missing ingredient is a ",
 StyleBox["fundamental diagram",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " \[LongDash] an empirical relation between density and flow. The simplest, \
due to Greenshields (1935), is linear in the speed:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0d0c5142-e1e8-40b4-8827-0424e3d438a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Q", "(", "\[Rho]", ")"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox["v", "max"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", "-", 
      FractionBox["\[Rho]", 
       SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "max"]]}], ")"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"6f717878-5b1f-4419-8e0f-e67af4fafb30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "so that flow is zero both at empty road (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", 
    RowBox[{"=", "0"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "d4a57478-7fbc-4585-ac7b-02d884b05ecb"],
 ") and at bumper-to-bumper jam (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "=", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "max"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "7e484c04-5c9a-49e2-ab04-1d3705ebd7ae"],
 ") and is maximised at the critical density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "c"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "max"], "/", "2"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "8b41a9b8-97e1-49ab-a123-613ac96077b8"],
 ". Substituting into the conservation law makes it formally a ",
 StyleBox["Burgers-type",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " equation \[LongDash] a scalar conservation law with a nonlinear flux. \
Characteristic speeds are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "Q", "/", "\[PartialD]", "\[Rho]"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "a01f4be4-e986-4154-959a-91567f705949"],
 "; they're positive (downstream) at low density and ",
 StyleBox["negative",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (upstream) at high density. A shock forms the moment two characteristics \
collide, and the shock's own speed is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["Q", "L"], "-", 
     SubscriptBox["Q", "R"]}], ")", "/", "(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "L"], "-", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Rho]", "R"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "1443842d-c80e-499d-82ce-07e65bf84f59"],
 " (the Rankine\[Dash]Hugoniot condition from gas dynamics)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2a8ae6cf-3c0e-4846-b163-19b72d502c02"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We discretise with the Godunov upwind flux, the textbook choice for \
Burgers-type equations. A CFL condition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]t", "\[LessEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]x", "/", 
     SubscriptBox["v", "max"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "374f3921-92f3-4687-b086-8b15b48a3016"],
 " keeps the scheme stable:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3a0ae045-b49c-40a0-8781-aebcdd6b7c8f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
lwrRes = LWR`SimulateLWR[];
LWR`PlotLWR[lwrRes]\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"948ab367-30ee-4250-a873-68780a6f3a86"],

