Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9. Network-level assignment: Wardrop equilibrium", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"589569a2-4ee1-4fb7-aaff-1e6c34837b29"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Zooming all the way back out: at the scale of a whole city, the question is \
no longer \"what does one link look like?\" but \"how do drivers distribute \
themselves across the network?\". Wardrop's first principle (1952) gives the \
answer: at equilibrium, all used paths between the same origin-destination \
pair have equal cost. No driver can unilaterally improve by switching routes. \
Formally, for all paths ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "q"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "274e23fa-2bfd-4cab-9897-b66210c8df52"],
 " used by the same OD pair:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"028e6d30-f8e9-43b2-a3e6-231e3c6527f8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["c", "p"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["c", "q"], "\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
   "\[ForAll]", " ", "used", " ", "paths", " ", "p", ",", " ", "q"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"3bfc99bb-2fc9-468f-9031-e24ecbfd2c46"],

Cell["\<\
Beckmann (1956) showed this is equivalent to the unique minimiser of the \
convex program\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bc640a6b-d0f8-4302-ba38-2b73cbf0cf88"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["min", "x"], " ", 
   RowBox[{
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     RowBox[{"e", "\[Element]", "E"}], ""], " ", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", 
     SubscriptBox["x", "e"]], " ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["t", "e"], "(", "\[Omega]", ")"}], 
    RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "\[Omega]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"a1529a53-a096-4e86-8c65-35b4d18fcabc"],

Cell["with the empirical Bureau of Public Roads link-cost function", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b3b4dc10-2670-4242-b6dc-163d8edda392"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["t", "e"], "(", 
    SubscriptBox["x", "e"], ")"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["t", "e", "0"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"1", "+", 
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
         FractionBox[
          SubscriptBox["x", "e"], 
          SubscriptBox["C", "e"]], ")"}], "\[Beta]"]}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"20169d33-068d-4033-acd6-1f27aa704379"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["t", "e", "0"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "57d11953-9be2-47fd-8ec5-cd40180776c9"],
 " is the free-flow travel time, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["C", "e"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "352c3b43-2239-4e3a-8a86-e61114b4e1d1"],
 " the capacity, and the tuning parameters are the canonical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", 
    RowBox[{"=", "0.15"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "07e09675-2159-45b2-953d-2f6d9b1ec8fe"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Beta]", 
    RowBox[{"=", "4"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "c6b0e5aa-d784-4f1d-a402-f52d2bf943f0"],
 ". Beckmann's integral is smooth and strictly convex, so ",
 StyleBox["FindMinimum", "Input"],
 " with an interior-point method converges in a handful of iterations. It's \
worth noting the economics here: Wardrop's user-equilibrium is ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the system optimum \[LongDash] the selfish route choice is in general \
suboptimal in the total-travel-time sense. The ratio of the two, the ",
 StyleBox["price of anarchy",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", is bounded above by 4/3 for BPR-style costs (Roughgarden 2002). A \
striking corollary is ",
 StyleBox["Braess's paradox",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": adding a road to a network can make ",
 StyleBox["everyone",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " slower. The constrained Aberdeen topology is exactly the kind of network \
where Braess-like effects show up."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8ed8ea41-6ce3-49d6-a87d-19be542e42c3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
naRes = NetworkAssignment`SimulateAssignment[];
NetworkAssignment`PlotAssignment[naRes]\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"fbead07f-7716-4889-989e-fd19ae4519b5"],

