Cell["\<\
Union Street (saturation 3.0\[Times] capacity) and Anderson Drive south (2.4\
\[Times]) emerge as the dominant bottlenecks, exactly the corridors \
Aberdonians complain about. The model has no knowledge of these being the \
busy corridors \[LongDash] they fall out of the Wardrop equilibrium purely \
from the network topology, link capacities, and OD demand.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8bdc88ab-265e-4901-b6ca-a2938a96b3db"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10. Time-varying demand", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d091cb50-b198-40bc-9934-ce211102f86a"],

Cell["\<\
Real traffic isn't a static snapshot: rush-hour demand builds up over 30\
\[Dash]60 minutes, peaks, and decays. A quick way to capture this without \
switching to a full dynamic traffic assignment (DTA) model is to solve \
Wardrop period by period, with some fraction of each period's flow carrying \
over as residual congestion that reduces the effective capacity in the next \
period:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b83a064-9bd2-4e12-8526-7c0b766b92e4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
daRes = DynamicAssignment`SimulateDynamicAssignment[];
DynamicAssignment`PlotDynamicAssignment[daRes]\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"94311c60-28e2-4162-920a-0527b882dfdc"],

