Cell[TextData[{
 "Three qualitative features of real rush hours fall out naturally: (a) flow \
on the ",
 StyleBox["shortest route",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " saturates first; (b) flow then ",
 StyleBox["spills over",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " onto secondary routes as the fastest route's BPR cost climbs; and (c) the \
link-cost heatmap decays ",
 StyleBox["asymmetrically",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " after the demand peak, because residual congestion from the peak persists \
into the post-peak period even as new demand is falling. This hysteresis is a \
well-known empirical fact on real motorways (the afternoon rush clears slower \
than the morning rush arrived), and it comes out of the coupling between \
demand and capacity without any explicit dynamical ingredients."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"663c7420-4542-4428-82e0-5653658fec24"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["11. Stitching it all together: OSM-based Aberdeen", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3083a31a-6320-43bf-8a58-ce9093f49255"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The repo ships two larger simulations that combine ingredients from almost \
every previous section. They're omitted from the attached bundle because they \
need OpenStreetMap JSON caches (1\[Dash]9 MB), but the pre-rendered \
animations are below for reference; see ",
 ButtonBox["github.com/mthiel74/TrafficJAms",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/mthiel74/TrafficJAms"], None}],
 " for the code."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1efd1cb4-0de6-4a05-b7e2-d3fb1fed93f1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 StyleBox["city-centre simulation",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (",
 StyleBox["AberdeenCityNetwork.wl", "Input"],
 ") parses a 1.3 MB Overpass extract around Marischal College into a \
1397-node / 2773-edge drivable graph, then runs 150 IDM agents routed by ",
 StyleBox["FindShortestPath", "Input"],
 " with on-arrival re-routing. It takes ~1 s wall time and reproduces the \
morning-rush pattern around Union Street pretty well:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"48df8906-658d-46ca-9a0e-edfd43ab93a5"],

